<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S4.T5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Parameter sensitivity and information compression for Layers 19-21 using SPD.</span>
A higher coefficient of variation indicates gradient stability,
a high gradient norm indicates high optimization sensitivity and
KL divergence quantifies information loss.
Vanilla Mamba shows a Layer 20 bottleneck (low gradient, high KL). Steering partially redistributes sensitivity but retains elevated KL, while Stable-Mamba exhibits more uniform sensitivity, higher gradients, and reduced KL, indicating bottleneck mitigation.</span></figcaption>
